f927f2a8-dade-4f74-962b-988b5e552565,"Boße, Sophie : {https://orcid.org/0009-0002-6461-8291} * Mazón, Elena Rey : {https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4813-5927} * Sennhenn, Anne : {https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3814-8774} * Vedder, Lucia : {https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8924-9800} * Schneider, Gabriel : {https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6573-3115}",CC-BY-4.0,https://doi.org/10.4126/FRL01-006490238 ,Metadata in agrosystem research practice ,FAIRagro (S),"This practical guide to collecting metadata in agricultural research aims to provide an easy and practice-oriented introduction to the world of data documentation. A decision tree guides researchers with simple, practical questions through the topics: 1 Why data should be documented; 2 Which forms and formats are appropriate for data documentation in your own project; 3 Which metadata should be collected for your own research data; 4 How the metadata can be created; 5 Which forms of storage and linking with the research data should be considered; and 6 How the quality of the metadata can be ensured. In addition to the decision tree, this document also contains brief explanations of terms (Appendix I) that should be understood in order to answer the questions in the decision tree meaningfully. In addition, a metadata guide (Appendix II) with many agricultural science examples provides an overview of metadata, metadata schemas, terminologies and various forms of metadata collection and storage. Internal links in the decision tree refer to specific term explanations or further explanations in the metadata guide. An interactive version of the decision tree was made by Justus Schneider: https://fairagro.github.io/metadata_decision_tree/index.html The metadata guide is adapted from Australian Research Data Commons (ARDC), ""ARDC Metadata Guide"", 1 March 2020, Zenodo. doi: 10.5281/ZENODO.6459832, licenced under CC BY 4.0 ",https://w3id.org/kim/hochschulfaechersystematik/n003,.pdf * .docx * .odt,Data Documentation * Agricultural Research Data * Research Data Management * Decision Tree * Metadata * Practical Guide,de * en,https://w3id.org/kim/hcrt/questionnaire * https://w3id.org/kim/hcrt/text,text,novice * advanced beginner,2025,student (MA) * student (PhD) * researcher * content provider,isSupplementedBy:https://doi.org/10.4126/FRL01-006511267 * isBasedOn:https://doi.org/10.5281/ZENODO.6459832,,1.0
44e198e8-8dbb-414d-8809-77c0da09e11c,"Boße, Sophie : {https://orcid.org/0009-0002-6461-8291} * Mazón, Elena Rey : {https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4813-5927} * Sennhenn, Anne : {https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3814-8774} * Vedder, Lucia : {https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8924-9800} * Schneider, Gabriel : {https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6573-3115}",CC-BY-4.0,https://doi.org/10.4126/FRL01-006511267,Metadata guide for agrosystem science,FAIRagro (S),"This practical guide to collecting metadata in agricultural research provides an easy, practical introduction to data documentation. It offers a straightforward, generic, workinglevel overview of the needs, issues, and processes related to metadata collection and creation in research. FAIRagro adapted the guide to the typical data types in agrosystem research. This guide can be used in combination with an interactive decision tree to clarify personal working steps for proper data documentation. It is based on: Australian Research Data Commons (ARDC) (2020). ARDC Metadata Guide. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6459832 [Titel anhand dieser DOI in Citavi-Projekt übernehmen] ",https://w3id.org/kim/hochschulfaechersystematik/n004,.pdf * .docx * .odt,Data Documentation * Agricultural Research Data * Research Data Management * Metadata * Practical Guide,de * en,https://w3id.org/kim/hcrt/questionnaire * https://w3id.org/kim/hcrt/text,text,novice * advanced beginner,2025,student (MA) * student (PhD) * researcher * content provider,isSupplementTo:https://doi.org/10.4126/FRL01-006490238 * isBasedOn:https://doi.org/10.5281/ZENODO.6459832,,1.0
